# dump_tex_bsp — system overview
# A report generator for Soldier of Fortune maps: read the texture lump and the
# entity table of every .bsp, then list the textures and sounds each map needs.
# Zones run left to right: entry points -> core -> state -> external.
# Style classes set strokes only, so light and dark stay readable.

title: |md
  # dump_tex_bsp
  Walks a tree of Soldier of Fortune .bsp files and reports which textures and sounds every map references — a restore list for a map archive.
| {near: top-center}

direction: right
grid-columns: 2
grid-rows: 2
horizontal-gap: 110
vertical-gap: 100

entry: Entry points {
  direction: down

  allmaps: `allmaps.py` · driver: walk every `.bsp` under a hardcoded Windows path, wipe the output dir, write eight report folders
  lib: `bsp_parse.py` · the library: lump reader, texture lister, entity-table sound finder
  gen: `ignorelist.py` · one-off: turn a resource tree into the two ignore lists
  knobs: module globals `SILENT`, `LOGGING`, `DEBUG`, `EXISTSCHECK`, `EXISTSPATH` · edited in the source, no flags
}

core: Core {
  direction: down

  magic: magic and version · `IBSP` at offset 0, version at 4, a warning if it is not 46
  lump: `grab_lump` · header is 8 B, then 8-byte offset/size pairs, returns a memoryview slice
  tex: `dump_textures` · lump 5, 76-byte surface headers, name at +40 as 32 B latin-1, forced to `.m32`
  ent: entity table · lump 0 decoded latin-1 and split into lines
  field: `grabField` and `grabFields` · find a classname, walk to its brace, pull one field out
  snd: `find_sounds` · `trigger_useable` keeps only `.wav`, `target_speaker` gets `.wav` appended
  exist: `EXISTSCHECK` · optional `os.path.isfile` against the texture and sound tree of that map
  defaults: ignore lists · every stock SoF asset filtered out, so only map content remains
  report: `allmaps.py` writes · `textures`, `sound`, `entlists`, `*_exist` and `*_missing` per map

  magic -> lump
  lump -> tex: two of the twenty-odd lumps are read
  lump -> ent
  ent -> field -> snd: one field per classname, two classnames total
  tex -> defaults
  snd -> defaults
  defaults -> exist: only survivors are checked on disk
  exist -> report
}

state: State {
  direction: down

  ignoretex: `ignore_defaults_tex.txt` · JSON array of lowercased relative texture paths {shape: cylinder}
  ignoresnd: `ignore_defaults_sound.txt` · the same for sound paths {shape: cylinder}
  rar: `bspdata.rar` · 2.6 MB of an earlier report from this tool, committed to the repo {shape: cylinder}
  out: output tree named by the first argument · deleted and rebuilt on every run {shape: cylinder}
}

ext: External {
  direction: down

  maps: `*.bsp` · SoF IBSP v46 maps, in a directory tree the walker mirrors
  base: resource tree `base/textures`, `base/sound` · what EXISTSCHECK stats, at a hardcoded Windows path
  stdlib: Python 3 stdlib only · `struct`, `memoryview`, `json`, `shutil`, nothing to install
  operator: a person · reads the report folders and diffs two runs by hand, nothing automates that
}

entry -> core: the driver passes each map path to the library
core -> state: two ignore lists in, one report tree out
core -> ext: reads maps and optionally stats their assets

classes: {
  entry: {style: {stroke: "#2f6fbf"}}
  core: {style: {stroke: "#2f8f5f"}}
  state: {style: {stroke: "#a86a12"; stroke-dash: 3}}
  ext: {style: {stroke: "#8a4fbf"; stroke-dash: 5}}
}

entry.class: entry
core.class: core
state.class: state
ext.class: ext
